The first four columns are of the lazy run, where every operation the layer defers is a node. `deferred fused`, `at once
fused`: in the fused run, the operations still written as nodes, and the calls and writes made as the program wrote them
because they were small. `expr.`: expressions of two operations or more found in the fused run's graphs. `tiled`: those
a program of kernel calls was planned for. `fused nodes`: nodes computed inside a program instead of by a call of their
own. `given up`: programs not run, or dropped, because of the arrays' layout or a floating-point exception NumPy reports.
`writes in place`, `copied`: deferred writes of the fused run made into the array's own memory, and into a copy of it.
`MB written`: the new arrays the calls wrote; a write into an array that exists is not counted.

